{
  "domain": "farming",
  "notes": "Seeds are split by patch type (allotment, herb, flower, hops, bush, tree, hardwood, fruit-tree, special); seed and sapling types come from name lists because the wiki only has flat \"Seeds\"/\"Saplings\" categories. Hops seeds include flax/hemp/cotton and hardwood seeds include camphor/ironwood/rosewood (both confirmed on the wiki). Mithril/Adamant seeds (flower gambling) are excluded from seed/farming. Family tags (trees, fruit trees, herbs, grape, flax/hemp/cotton, seaweed, coral, kebbit, larupia, graahk, kyatt, antelope) sit under the shared material root and match broadly by name so they also catch other domains’ items of the family (logs, planks, bows, flatpacks, grimy/clean herbs, unf potions, outfits); the merge should union these rules with other proposals’ rules for the same key. The magic tree family uses key magic-tree because magic is the skill tag; orange and curry use exact name lists to avoid the colour (Orange cape/dye/feather) and the Curry dish. No family tags for allotment, bush, flower or hop crops (each would only cover a seed and one crop; the seed/produce type tags already group them). fur sits under hunter-drop, so non-Hunter furs (Bear fur, Grey wolf fur, Fur, Jaguar fur) also get hunter. Metal tiers on axes/pickaxes are left to the equipment/smithing proposal (the items carry Bronze..Rune categories). woodcutting/mining/fishing have no direct rule here; production proposals may add logs/ores/raw fish. Spirit, hespori, crystal and anima seeds are not GE-tradeable, and only Bird nest (empty)/Crushed nest exist on the GE (nest contents like seeds and rings are tagged by their own types).",
  "tags": [
    {
      "key": "farming",
      "label": "Farming",
      "parent": "skilling",
      "description": "Seeds, saplings, produce, compost and farming tools",
